+## Canonical input/archive source closure (SOL-BOUNDARY carrier)
+
+Before the canonical input is materialized, `build_v3.py` now authenticates all three
+manifest dimensions (`base.sha256`, `base.bytes`, and `base.files`) and decodes regular
+files into memory only after each tar member has a canonical relative POSIX name.
+Absolute, parent-escaping, backslash, duplicate-normalized, special, sparse, oversized,
+and regular-file-prefix-colliding members fail before any filesystem write. This is the
+*input* boundary; atomic/non-empty handling for `--tree` remains a separate publication
+lane.
+
+The source receipt now includes the executing `build_v3.py`, `apply_v3.py`, and the
+source-only closure contracts as well as package overlays. Run the predecessor killers
+from this directory under both interpreter modes:
+
+```bash
+python -m unittest -v source_checks/test_build_v3_closure.py
+python -O -m unittest -v source_checks/test_build_v3_closure.py
+```
